<p>A young humpback whale nicknamed Timmy was released into the North Sea off Denmark on Saturday after weeks stranded in shallow waters near Germany’s Baltic coast and being towed in a water-filled barge, rescuers and witnesses said. The whale had been seen near Germany’s Baltic Sea coast on March 3, far from humpbacks’ usual Atlantic habitat, and its condition worsened after repeated strandings near Wismar and other shallow areas. A private rescue initiative moved the animal toward deeper water after Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania’s environment minister approved the plan, despite warnings from some marine experts that the operation could further stress an already weakened whale and that its chances of survival were low. Jens Schwarck, a member of the initiative, told German news agency dpa that the whale was released at about 9 a.m. local time around 70 kilometers from Skagen, Denmark; several reports said its condition after release and the reliability of tracking data were not immediately clear.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/LHW2T5aUA4EAttExifquyHQbOMx1yXMZIX-qhb8V7WwsYo6lesWbJH9DPvrHarSFa6WIvwJ3_eKZxpKsG_naz8MCGnEDJ3j9DCg3ByNKbZUiFlZskUP1zzfxkzcR33Cjaxsp-2cLIIaET7pZaHbTpGEUPgkCSfxl2c4azUYGs7bUORH5WZMX-w_dfvqQj5i0YGWMoiD3inCHXxCliSQuFmfMNOhSfpxPVEuN6K-IOD659dX6LUjBTOUpVyn2a-7RxwPu' alt='The humpback whale Timmy was released at sea after weeks stranded near Germany’s Baltic coast.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Transport conditions: The convoy paused near Denmark’s northern tip because waves of about 2 meters could have further injured the whale inside the barge.</li><li>Public attention: Timmy’s strandings and rescue attempts were livestreamed and widely followed online, while activists protested on Wismar’s beach, calling for the whale to be moved back toward open ocean.</li><li>Video evidence: Drone footage showed a whale swimming and spouting near the barge after the release, although dpa said it had not immediately confirmed the animal was Timmy.</li><li>Animal size: Several reports described Timmy as roughly 12 meters long and about 12 tons; one account estimated the whale’s age at 4 to 6 years.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania environment authorities: State Environment Minister Till Backhaus said the transport should continue farther into the North Sea while the whale remained aboard, because each additional kilometer would give it a better start. (<a href='https://nos.nl/l/2612719'>NOS</a>)</li><li>Ocean Museum Germany: TV 2 Denmark said discussion at one stage turned to displaying the whale if it died; director Burkard Baschek said the rescue was not worth the effort. (<a href='https://nyheder.tv2.dk/samfund/2026-05-02-timmy-er-fri-historisk-redningsaktion-er-slut'>TV 2 Denmark</a>)</li><li>Veterinary team: Anne Herrschaft said after Timmy swam toward deeper water that the farewell was painful because the team had repeatedly feared losing the whale, but that seeing it free made her happy. (<a href='https://www.abc.es/sociedad/logran-liberar-timmy-ballena-varada-alemania-marzo-20260502171907-nt.html'>ABC</a>)</li><li>Rescue sponsors: TV 2 Denmark, citing AFP, said two wealthy backers financed the plan that made the barge operation possible. (<a href='https://nyheder.tv2.dk/samfund/2026-05-02-timmy-er-fri-historisk-redningsaktion-er-slut'>TV 2 Denmark</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/05/02/humpback-whale-stranded-in-germany-released-into-north-sea'>Humpback whale stranded in Germany released into North Sea</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/02/world/europe/timmy-whale-germany-released.html'>Timmy the Stranded Whale Is Released After an Elaborate Rescue</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/2/timmy-the-humpback-whale-escapes-to-the-north-sea'>Timmy the humpback whale escapes to the North Sea</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news